{
  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 is a dramatically better RNA encoder than pca_n2000 or scgpt (0.7150 vs ~0.62 vs ~0.52), and avgpool+concat is the best aggregation/fusion combination. The only untested high-impact variable in the scvi_n200 context is the image encoder: we've only tested scvi_n200 with imagenet_vit_l. With pca_n2000, vit_l and resnet50 were close (0.6287 vs 0.6186), so it's unclear whether vit_l's advantage persists or reverses when paired with the richer scvi_n200 representations. Config_015 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + concat) directly tests this. If resnet50 matches or beats vit_l, it broadens the search; if vit_l is clearly superior, we can confidently lock in the image encoder and spend remaining budget on finer refinements (e.g., fusion weighting or profile setting). This is the highest-information experiment for the 3 remaining slots."
}

